    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup centers around the reliability of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who commands the highest score of the day at 67.81. Despite facing a lefty in Newcomb, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintains a strong dynamic platoon edge (+2%) and a favorable batting order position (#2), shielding him from the volatility seen in other spots. **Will Smith** follows closely with a 60.27 efficiency score; his placement in the #3 hole combined with a solid 0.389 xwOBA against Mahle suggests he remains the anchor of our lineup for this slate, benefiting from a 4% dynamic platoon boost that validates his inclusion as a primary producer.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Braden Montgomery**, who clocked in at 34.24. While his switch-hitting utility and 100% recency trend kept him on our radar, the matchup against Espino (2.51 xERA) effectively neutralized his value. The SP skill penalty (-19%) proved insurmountable, keeping him below our \"Zebras Floor\" of 40.0. Elsewhere, **Jonathan Aranda** occupies a marginal 47.46 slot; his score is hampered significantly by a -12% platoon penalty against Fried, though his #2 order spot and a park factor bump (+4%) keep him in the mix to avoid depleting our game cap reserves. With **Cal Raleigh**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Yainer Diaz** all off the schedule, we are banking on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** to carry the offensive load against high-caliber arms. We are monitoring the **Jonathan Aranda** spot closely, as his struggle against lefties represents our primary risk factor heading into first pitch.",
